WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:03.000
A French story, “Le phare de Kerlann”, is added and set to be translated into English.

00:03.000 --> 00:04.500
Coglossa shows each step as it works: reading, the guide, translating, checking.

00:04.500 --> 00:11.000
Done. The summary says one passage of five is worth a quick look.

00:11.000 --> 00:16.000
Passage 4 opens with the reason it was flagged: the meaning may have shifted.

00:16.000 --> 00:21.000
A person types a better translation and saves it. It is marked as checked.

00:21.000 --> 00:23.500
“Always translate Kerlann as Kerlann” is applied to the whole set.

00:23.500 --> 00:29.000
Coglossa rechecks the document against the updated guide.

00:29.000 --> 00:32.000
The translation guide now lists Kerlann as a term that is always used as written.

00:32.000 --> 00:36.600
The finished translation can be downloaded as Word, a side-by-side Word file or a web page.
